+// REWINDBOX_ZCULL_CONSERVATIVE_627: the mode where no report ever makes anything wait. A
+// queued report is written at once with a value that reads "visible", no page is locked,
+// no label waits, and the GPU result replaces it when the query completes, in the usual
+// update() pass. A guest that reads the report before that gets "visible" and draws the
+// object; one that reads it later gets the real value. It differs from Relaxed ZCULL
+// Sync, which leaves the previous bytes of the slot in place (Assassin's Creed BLES00158,
+// Build 612: torches and lights flickered). Whether a guest can see the difference between
+// "visible" and the real value is a device question: off for every title by default, and
+// the ZCULL On-Demand Reads lever keeps exact values.
